<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Admin | Registration | {{siteName}}</title>
    {{>partials/head-deps.hbs}}
    {{>partials/head-styles.hbs}}
</head>
<body>
{{>partials/admin-shell.hbs}}
    <h1>Registration</h1>
    {{#saved}}<div class="alert alert-success" role="alert">Settings saved.</div>{{/saved}}
    <p class="text-secondary">Control whether visitors can create their own accounts on this site.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/a/registration" class="edit-form">
        {{{csrfField}}}
        {{^mailConfiguredForRegistration}}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
            Self-service registration requires email to be configured. Set up
            SMTP on the <a href="/a/mail">Mail</a> settings page first. Self-registration will not be available, even if enabled below,
            until this is configured.
        </div>
        {{/mailConfiguredForRegistration}}
        <div class="form-check mb-3">
            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="registrationEnabled" value="1" {{#registrationEnabled}}checked{{/registrationEnabled}}>
            <label class="form-check-label">Allow visitors to create their own accounts</label>
        </div>
        <p class="form-text">Off by default (wiki is private and only admins create logins; when on, a “Create an account” link appears on the sign-in page and anyone, except as specified below, can register at <code>/register</code>).</p>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Allowed email domains <span class="text-secondary">(optional)</span></label>
            <input class="form-control" type="text" name="registrationAllowedDomains" value="{{registrationAllowedDomainsValue}}" placeholder="e.g. example.com, example.org">
            <p class="form-text">Restrict sign-ups to these email domains (comma- or space-separated). Leave blank to allow any address.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Default group for new accounts</label>
            <select class="form-select" name="registrationDefaultGroup">
                {{#registrationGroupOptions}}<option value="{{value}}" {{#selected}}selected{{/selected}}>{{label}}</option>{{/registrationGroupOptions}}
            </select>
            <p class="form-text">Group each new account is added to. With “None”, registrants still get read-everywhere access via the built-in “User” group by default, but verify the configuration of the Users group in your environment for exact permissions if using.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="form-check mb-3">
            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="registrationRequireApproval" value="1" {{#registrationRequireApproval}}checked{{/registrationRequireApproval}}>
            <label class="form-check-label">Require administrator approval of new accounts</label>
        </div>
        <p class="form-text">When on, a confirmed account can't sign in until an admin approves it on the <a href="/a/users">Users</a> page, which will appear after user confirms email address. When off, confirming the email activates the account immediately.</p>

        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
    </form>
{{>partials/admin-shell-end.hbs}}
{{{bodyHtml}}}</body>
</html>
